<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yellow Turban Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">184 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yellow Turban Rebellion was a large peasant uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> that began in 184 CE, led by the Taoist faith healer Zhang Jue and his brothers. Driven by millenarian expectations and agrarian distress, it spread across much of northern China. Although suppressed, it greatly strengthened regional warlords, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> treat it as a major step towards the dynasty's collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yellow-turban-rebellion.jpg" alt="Yellow Turban Rebellion" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellow_Turban_Rebellion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
